    </track></source></video></div>
</div>


<para>An imaginary line that a function value will not touch or cross is called an <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">asymptote</term>.</para>
<para>The value of the range that the function will never touch is called the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">horizontal asymptote</term>. </para>
<para>In the function graphed, the horizontal asymptote is \(y=0\).</para></section>
